{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108130","id":2627783820,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6coMyM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108130","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108130.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108130.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108130","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108130/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108130/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108130/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/51f2e829b75ea376368cb88910c0ece062f27164","number":108130,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `AHashMap` for scalability","user":{"login":"Brogolem35","id":29329606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzI5NjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29329606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35","html_url":"https://github.com/Brogolem35","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Brogolem35/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"In this PR, I implemented some of the optimizations used in abseil's SwissTable ([1](https://abseil.io/about/design/swisstables), [2](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ncHmEUmJZf4), [3](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JZE3_0qvrMg)).\r\n\r\n# Optimizations Made\r\n\r\n1. Tag (metadata) is 1 byte. Tag and position to element are stored in seperate arrays (SoA over AoS).\r\n2. The 8 leftmost bits of the hash are used as tag. The whole hash is used for the finding of the probe.\r\n3. Deletion uses tombstones.\r\n4. Growth rate is increased from 2 times to 4 times.\r\n\r\n# Differences from abseil's implementation\r\n\r\n- abseil's implementation uses the rightmost 7 bits for the tag, and rest of the 57 bits for probe finding.\r\n- abseil prioritizes insertion and finding speed of its implementation over iteration, but in our case, iteration speed is one of the key factors. Thus, elements are still stored in a dense array.\r\n- This implementation **does not** make use of **SIMD** intrinsics, but opens the gates to it. Even without the SIMD, it outperforms the old implementation on middle to large size hashmaps (la. Benchmarks), and addition of the SIMD can be done on another PR.\r\n\r\n# Benchmarks\r\n\r\nTest code is from #106996 \r\n\r\n[swiss_int16.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972982/swiss_int16.txt)\r\n[swiss_int64.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972983/swiss_int64.txt)\r\n[swiss_variant.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972984/swiss_variant.txt)\r\n[master_int16.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972987/master_int16.txt)\r\n[master_int64.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972988/master_int64.txt)\r\n[master_variant.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20972989/master_variant.txt)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id"